  "note": "Election of the Limavady Urban District Council, polled Wednesday 16 October 1946 (Belfast News-Letter, 18 October 1946, p. 6). The queue round is dated 18 September; the poll was a month later. Thirteen candidates for nine seats — the first contest in eighteen years. Eight Unionist nominees, four Independents and one ex-Servicemen's representative. Percentage poll 81; nine spoiled votes."
